---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { githubUrl } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy | Shadow"
  description="What Shadow and this website collect, and what they never see: your code stays end to end encrypted."
  path="privacy/"
  home={false}
>
  <Prose eyebrow="Privacy" title="What Shadow can and can’t see">
    <h2>Your code</h2>
    <p>
      Files in a Shadow session are encrypted with <code class="inline-code">AES-256-GCM</code> on your machine before they are sent.
      The key lives in the invite link after the <code class="inline-code">#</code>, which is never sent to the relay,
      so the relay only handles ciphertext. Shadow has no accounts, so there is no profile, email, or password to store.
    </p>

    <h2>The Mac app</h2>
    <p>
      The menu bar app sends a small set of anonymous usage events to PostHog so the maintainer can see whether sessions
      start and where they fail. Events include app launches, session starts, joins, stops with their duration,
      invite copies, read only mode, and error categories. They never include file contents, file names, folder paths,
      or the invite link. Screen views and lifecycle autocapture are turned off.
    </p>

    <h2>The CLI and VS Code extension</h2>
    <p>
      The CLI and the VS Code extension do not include analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses PostHog to measure page views and how the page gets used, such as clicks on the download,
      copy, and demo controls. It does not create profiles for anonymous visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Check it yourself</h2>
    <p>
      Shadow is open source under the MIT license. Every claim on this page can be verified in the{' '}
      <a href={githubUrl} class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">source on GitHub</a>.
      Questions or concerns? <a href={`${githubUrl}/issues`} class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open an issue</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
